{"id": "tea:darsana-upanisad:1.1-5", "source": "src:darsana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.1-5"}, "paraphrase": "Dattātreya, the four-armed Mahāviṣṇu, teaches his disciple Sāṅkṛti the eight-limbed yoga.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "teachers": ["tch:dattatreya", "tch:sankrti"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:darsana-upanisad:1.21-22", "source": "src:darsana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.21-22"}, "paraphrase": "The body is utterly impure, the embodied Self utterly pure; one who abandons the purity of knowledge for external purity abandons gold for a clod.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ethics", "ultimate"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:darsana-upanisad:1.6-24", "source": "src:darsana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.6-24"}, "paraphrase": "Ten yamas are defined twice over — outwardly and inwardly: non-injury is not harming (except as the Veda enjoins), and supremely, knowing the Self as all-pervading; truth is speech that is true, and supremely 'all is Brahman'; purity is external, and inward as 'I am pure'.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["ethics", "ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:ten-yamas-ten-niyamas"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:darsana-upanisad:10", "source": "src:darsana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "10"}, "paraphrase": "Samādhi is the knowledge of the unity of jīva and the supreme; the Self appears divided only through māyā; 'I am not the body… I am Śiva alone'; seeing all beings in the Self, Sāṅkṛti abides fearless.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "karma-liberation"], "paths": ["pth:darsana-eight-limbs"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:darsana-upanisad:2.1-16", "source": "src:darsana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.1-16"}, "paraphrase": "Ten niyamas (austerity, contentment, faith, charity, worship of the Lord, hearing the settled doctrine, modesty, discernment, japa, vows); worship of the Lord is a heart free of passion, speech free of falsehood, action free of violence; japa is spoken (loud or whispered) or mental, the whispered worth a thousand loud, the mental a thousand whispered.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["ethics", "practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:ten-yamas-ten-niyamas"], "practices": ["prc:japa-kinds"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:darsana-upanisad:3.1-13", "source": "src:darsana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "3.1-13"}, "paraphrase": "Nine postures — svastika, gomukha, padma, vīra, siṃha, bhadra, mukta, mayūra and sukha.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "practices": ["prc:asanas-yoga-upanisads"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:darsana-upanisad:4.35-38", "source": "src:darsana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "4.35-38"}, "paraphrase": "Deities of the channels: suṣumnā Śiva, iḍā Hari, piṅgalā Brahmā, and others.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:nadis"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:darsana-upanisad:4.39-47", "source": "src:darsana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "4.39-47"}, "paraphrase": "Time within the body: the moon moves in iḍā, the sun in piṅgalā; passage from piṅgalā to iḍā is the northern course, the reverse the southern; their junction is the new moon; the mūlādhāra and the head are the equinoxes; the eclipses happen within.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "cosmic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["body-layers", "world-fate"], "concepts": ["cpt:inner-time"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:darsana-upanisad:4.48-59", "source": "src:darsana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "4.48-59"}, "paraphrase": "The sacred places are in the body — Śrīparvata in the head, Kedāra on the forehead, Vārāṇasī between brows and nose, Kurukṣetra in the breast, Prayāga in the heart lotus, Cidambaram in the heart; one who leaves the inner tīrtha for the outer throws away a gem for glass; an impure mind is not cleansed by bathing, as a liquor pot is not by washing. Yogins see Śiva in the Self, not in images; images are imagined for the ignorant.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:inner-tirthas", "cpt:images-for-the-ignorant"], "disputes": ["dsp:image-worship-and-inner-worship"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:darsana-upanisad:4.6-13", "source": "src:darsana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "4.6-13"}, "paraphrase": "Fourteen channels are principal; the suṣumnā, the brahma-nāḍī along the spine (vīṇādaṇḍa), is chief; the kuṇḍalī lies below.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:nadis", "cpt:kundalini"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:darsana-upanisad:5.1-14", "source": "src:darsana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "5.1-14"}, "paraphrase": "Channels are purified by breath practice, with signs of lightness, digestive fire and inner sound; or the yogin may purify himself by the knowledge of the Self.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "practices": ["prc:nadi-sodhana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:darsana-upanisad:6.1-14", "source": "src:darsana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "6.1-14"}, "paraphrase": "Prāṇāyāma with the measures of a, u and m; grades of sweat, trembling and rising.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "practices": ["prc:pranava-dhyana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:darsana-upanisad:6.36-51", "source": "src:darsana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "6.36-51"}, "paraphrase": "Sounds of the conch, thunder and waterfall are heard in the brahmarandhra; by dispassion knowledge arises.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["sound-language", "powers-experiences"], "concepts": ["cpt:nada"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:darsana-upanisad:7", "source": "src:darsana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "7"}, "paraphrase": "Five pratyāhāras: forcibly withdrawing the senses; seeing all that is seen as the Self; offering all acts' fruits to Brahman; doing daily and occasional rites as worship of Brahman; and moving the breath through eighteen vital points and fixing it there, the self in the Self.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "practices": ["prc:five-pratyaharas", "prc:marmasthana-dharana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:darsana-upanisad:8", "source": "src:darsana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "8"}, "paraphrase": "Dhāraṇā: dissolving the outer elements into their places in the body with their syllables and deities — Brahmā earth, Viṣṇu water, Maheśa fire, Īśvara air, Sadāśiva space — or holding Śiva as the Person.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "practices": ["prc:element-dharanas"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:darsana-upanisad:9", "source": "src:darsana-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "9"}, "paraphrase": "Dhyāna: 'so'ham' — meditating on Maheśvara as oneself, 'I am' as being-consciousness-bliss.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice", "ultimate"], "practices": ["prc:saguna-nirguna-dhyana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
